From 841cd99eebbe47ef6175b1ed2300548a2bfe0c2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:03:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: remove the unreachable fail-rate tier from the Teleport
 Other defence

borg_defend_aux_tele_away() lowers the spell failure it accepts as the
danger rises: by 10 above three times the avoidance and by 5 above
twice the avoidance.  A third tier, reached through the else of the
"twice" test, raised the allowance by 5 when the danger was above five
halves of the avoidance.  A danger that is not above twice the
avoidance is never above five halves of it (the avoidance is never
negative), so that tier could never run.

Remove it.  No behaviour change.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#176.
---
 src/borg/borg-fight-defend.c | 4 ----
 1 file changed, 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-fight-defend.c b/src/borg/borg-fight-defend.c
index 05e6ac00e..3a71b1434 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-fight-defend.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-fight-defend.c
@@ -1147,10 +1147,6 @@ static int borg_defend_aux_tele_away(int p1)
         /* scary */
         if (p1 > borg.avoidance * 2)
             fail_allowed -= 5;
-        else
-            /* a little scary */
-            if (p1 > (borg.avoidance * 5) / 2)
-                fail_allowed += 5;
 
     /* do I have the ability? */
     if (borg_spell_okay_fail(TELEPORT_OTHER, fail_allowed)
-- 
